      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Echoing sentiment that this seems like a great use of the impostor system, allowing me to see roughly how people want to be seen under a wider variety of circumstances without it hitting my performance as hard. \n\nDiamonds are boring, grey robots already rob people enough of their identity before that and fall-backs while preferable to the former are still a step short of ideal. Most avatars don't have them and alternative fall-backs typically don't replicate tracking that accurately... Conversely, the impostors I've seen on random dancers have tracked way nicer than I thought they would! \n\nHaving essentially a LOD like system like this seems like it might be an enticing option, even if performance wise it wouldn't be as good as the more identity scrubbing types we have right now. \n\nSeeing random impostors in-game further convinced me that this'd be something I'd love to see. Knowing its the closest thing to how that person wants to be seen feels really nice to me. Of course I still have options if I really don't like what I see...",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
